From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:26:33 -0700
Subject: Make singleton Persistents in css/ thread local

CSS parsing can happen on multiple threads. One example is canvas
context parsing, which is limited to a certain set of values for which
we have previously avoided general property parsing by not allowing
unparsed values. However, for the typed OM API CSSUnparsedValue, we can
parse arbitrary property values in if(supports()) like this:

CSSUnparsedValue(['if(supports(animation: a): 1px)']).toString();

In some cases we rely on static singletons which are sometimes allocated
on the oilpan heap, which can not be safely constructed or accessed
cross thread.

Introduce ThreadSpecific singletons for these.

Bug: 575201475, 575201060
Change-Id: I7a9e53999afd4b093f3ff0fcea88d0f9766536ca
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8608808
Reviewed-by: Michael Lippautz <mlippautz@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1724494}

